<language_name>Mingrelian (Samurzakano-Zugdidsky)</language_name>






    <headers>

<orthography_header>Native Orthography</orthography_header>
<alt_orthography_header>Mkhedruli (Georgian) Script</alt_orthography_header>
<IPA_header>Transcription</IPA_header>
<alt_IPA_header>Romanization</alt_IPA_header>
<gloss_header>Russian Gloss</gloss_header>
<alt_gloss_header>English Gloss</alt_gloss_header>

</headers>
    
<item>
<entry>1</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>რდუ ართი რჩინუ კოჩი.</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>rˈdə artʲ̥ rt͡ʃin k’ɔt͡ʃ̥</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>rdu arti rčinu ḳoči</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Был один старик. </gloss>
<alt_gloss>There was one old man.</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>2</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>თის ჸუნდჷ ართი სქუა მეჩხომე.</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>tʰis ˀund̥ artʲı̥ skua mɛt͡ʃχɔmɛ</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>tis ʽundə arti skua mečxome</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Он имел сына-рыбака. </gloss>
<alt_gloss>He had a son-a fisherman.</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>3</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>ართიშახ მეჩხომექ მიდართჷ ჩხომიშ ოჭოფუშა;</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>ˈʔartʲⁱ̥̆ ʃaχ ˈmɛt͡ʃχɔmɛkʰ miˈdartʰ t͡ʃχɔˈmiʃ ɔˈt͡ʃ’ɔpʃḁ</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>artišax mečxomek midartə čxomiš oč̣opuša</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Однажды рыбак ушел лобить рыбу.</gloss>
<alt_gloss>Once the fishman went to fish.</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>4</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>გილართჷ ბრელი, </alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>ɡilartʰ brɛɩlʲ⁽⁾</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>gilartə breli</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Ходил он долго, </gloss>
<alt_gloss>He walked far,</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>5</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>მარა ჩხომქ ვა აჭოფუ. </alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>mara t͡ʃχɔmkʿ ˈvaːt͡ʃ’ɔpʊ̥</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>mara čxomk va ač̣opu</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>но ничево не поймал. </gloss>
<alt_gloss>but caught nothing.</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>6</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>ბოლოს ოჭოფუ ართი ჭიჭე, მარა ძალამი სქვამი ჩხომი.</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>bɔlɔs ɔt͡ʃ’ɔpʊ̥ artʲi̥ t͡ʃ’it͡ʃ’ɛ mara ʣalamʲɩ̯̆ skvam̯ t͡ʃχɔmʲ̯</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>bolos oč̣opu arti č̣ič̣e mara ʒalami skvami čxomi</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Наконец, рыбак поймал одну маленькую, но очень красивую рыбку. </gloss>
<alt_gloss>At last, the fisherman caught one small, but very beautiful fish.</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>7</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>მეჩხომეს შეეცოდჷ ე ჩხომქ დო</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>mɛt͡ʃχɔmɛs ʃɛɛt͡sɔd ɛ t͡ʃχɔŋkʿ d̥ɔ</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>mečxomes šeecodə e čxomk do</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Рыбак пожалел рыбку </gloss>
<alt_gloss>The fisherman pitied the fish</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>8</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>ქიდნახუნუ წყარქ კონი.</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>kanaχunu t͡s’q’ars k’inʲı</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>kidnaxunu c̣q̣ars ḳoni</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>и отпустил ее.  </gloss>
<alt_gloss>and released her(it).</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>9</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>ჸუდეშა ქუმორთჷ-ნი, მუმაქ კითხუ:</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>ˈudɛʃa kʰəmərtʰənʲ muˈmak k’e̥tχ⁽⁾</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>ʽudeša kumortəni mumak ḳitxu</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Когда рыбак вернулся домой, отец спрасил:</gloss>
<alt_gloss>When the fisherman returned home, his father asked:</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>10</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>- ჩხომი ვა გიჭოფუნიავო?</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>t͡ʃχɔmʲ̥ va it͡ʃ’ɔpʰuniavɔ</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>čxomi va gič̣opuniavo</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>- Не поймал рыбы?</gloss>
<alt_gloss>You didn't catch fish?</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>11</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>სქუაქ უწუ:</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>skɥak ut͡s’u</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>skuak uc̣u</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>Сын ответил:</gloss>
<alt_gloss>The son answered:</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>12</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>- ართი ჩხომი ოპჭოფი,</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>artʲ̥ t͡ʃχɔmʲ ˀɔpt͡ʃ’ɔpʲı̥</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>arti čxomi op̣č̣opi</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>- Поймал одну рыбку, </gloss>
<alt_gloss>I caught one fish(dim.),</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>13</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>მარა ძალამი სქვამი რდჷ,</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>mara ʣalamʲ⁽⁾ sk’vamʲ rdə</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>mara alami skvami rdə</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>но она была очень красивая, </gloss>
<alt_gloss>but she(it) was very beautiful,</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
    
<item>
<entry>14</entry>
<native_orthography></native_orthography>
<alt_native_orthography>შემეცოდჷ დო კონი გუ̅ტევა.</alt_native_orthography>
<IPA_transcription>ʃɛmɛt͡sɔddɔ k’in ɡɔut’ɛva</IPA_transcription>
<alt_IPA_transcription>šemecodə do ḳoni gūṭeva</alt_IPA_transcription>
<gloss>я пожалел ее и отпустил.</gloss>
<alt_gloss>I pitied her(it) and released [her(it)].</alt_gloss>
<semantic_category></semantic_category>
</item>
</wordlist>